s in London.\n\n## The numbers you specifically asked for — do not print from me\n\nThe figure I carry is **51 hours over 16 days**, with work running roughly late July to late August 1851. But I also carry competing recollections of **52 hours** and **44 hours**, and I cannot reliably reconstruct the date range. I don't trust my own memory here to the precision a fact sheet implies, and this is the single most quotable number in your piece. Same caution on the \"about 25 minutes\" figure for the Chubb lock.\n\nThe authority is the **arbitrators' certificate**, which was reproduced in the contemporary record. Get the number from that document, not from a secondary retelling — the secondaries are where the 44/51/52 divergence comes from.\n\n## Source leads to verify — not citations\n\nThese are real works I'm confident exist and that treat this episode directly. Treat them as where to look, and build your citation from the copy in front of you:\n\n- **Charles Tomlinson (ed.), *Rudimentary Treatise on the Construction of Locks*, London: John Weale, 1853** — compiled from A. C. Hobbs's own papers. Primary-adjacent, and the source of the famous Hobbs line about rogues already knowing more than we can teach them.\n- **George Price, *A Treatise on Fire and Thief-Proof Depositories, and Locks and Keys*, London, 1856** — covers the controversy at length and is the usual quarry for the certificate text.\n- **Contemporary press, August 1851** — *The Times* and the *Illustrated London News* carried the dispute as it ran.\n\nBoth books are out of copyright and should be findable in full on the Internet Archive or Google Books, which means you can verify the hours, the days and the page numbers yourself in well under an hour.\n\n## Two traps worth avoiding in the copy\n\n1. **Don't merge the Chubb and Bramah openings.** They were different locks, different methods, different days.\n2. **Be careful with \"unpicked for N years.\"** You'll see 60, 67 and other figures, because writers silently pick different start dates for the challenge placard. Say what date you're counting from.\n\nIf you'd rather not do the checking yourself: grant web access in this session and I'll run the verification and hand you the fact sheet with real, checked citations — that's a much better outcome than what I can do blind, and it's quick.\n\nWant me to publish the verified version as a shareable page once the sources are confirmed?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":32672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":687},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eefc4cd3-d52f-4979-83b5-000f54e7f03b","uuid":"b64fde67-9f51-4d69-a8d8-8c61e1e975d7","timestamp":"2026-09-25T07:28:57.678Z","request_id":"req_011CfPmDM88r1MhfB2jfEEKL"}
